.pytest_cache/
# Large, regeneratable market-data pickle caches -- real market data
# re-fetched fresh from yfinance/Alpaca/IBKR by each research script's own
# fetch step, not authored work; committing these would bloat the repo
# with 100+MB of binary data that provides no value once the fetch script
# exists (found 2026-09-09 before a large commit/push).
*.pkl

# Logs, crash dumps, and raw data-cache files INSIDE research subdirectories
# (signals_research/, scalp_research/, daytrader_research/, etc.) -- the
# top-level ibkr_trader/backend/*.log-style patterns above only match files
# directly in backend/, not nested subdirectories, so this same class of
# file was slipping through in every *_research/ subfolder. Found 2026-09-09
# before a large commit: ~700MB of these (a 237MB tape_data.db, 60-145MB
# raw option-chain/bar JSON dumps, dozens of multi-MB crash logs) were about
# to get swept into git history permanently. Real research value is in the
# scripts + RESEARCH_LOG.md + summary CSVs, not these regeneratable dumps.
ibkr_trader/backend/**/*.log
ibkr_trader/backend/**/*.log.*
ibkr_trader/backend/**/*_stdout.txt
ibkr_trader/backend/**/*_stderr.txt
ibkr_trader/backend/**/*stdout*.log
ibkr_trader/backend/**/*stderr*.log
ibkr_trader/backend/**/crash_logs/
ibkr_trader/backend/**/*.db
ibkr_trader/backend/**/results.json
